  "question": {
    "text": "In the wet tests for identification of various cations by precipitation, which transition element cation doesn&#39;t belong to group IV in qualitative inorganic analysis?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Cations are segregated in 5 groups depending upon their solubility with the help of various precipitating reagents. As per the segregation,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Co</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Ni</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;belongs&nbsp;to the 4th group and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;belongs to the 3rd group.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  }
